--! A test platform's one capability: make every later `child_process.spawn`
--! fail with an error code of the caller's choosing, by the route Node
--! takes for that code, to reach the failures `ChildProcess.run` names
--! that no program can arrange by itself (no process to spare, no memory,
--! a busy file).

--| From now on, every `child_process.spawn` fails with an error whose
--| `code` is the given one: as the child's `error` event for `EACCES`,
--| `EAGAIN`, `EMFILE`, `ENFILE` and `ENOENT`, thrown for any other.
pub foreign impure failSpawns : String → ⊤
